{"name":"Urban Auburn","hex":"#7c4a2c","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"urban","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of, pertaining to, characteristic of, or happening or located in, a city or town; of, pertaining to, or characteristic of life in such a place, especially when contrasted with the countryside.","Living in a city or town."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/urban"},{"term":"auburn","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dark reddish-brown colour, often used to describe hair colour."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a reddish-brown colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/auburn"}],"entries":[{"title":"Auburn hair","blocks":[{"text":"Auburn hair is a human hair color, a variety of red hair, most commonly described as reddish-brown in color. Auburn hair ranges in shades from medium to dark. It can be found with a wide array of skin tones and eye colors. The chemical pigments that cause the coloration of auburn hair are often pheomelanin with high levels of eumelanin."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Uyghur-redhead.jpg/330px-Uyghur-redhead.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Auburn_hair"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Anthonis_Mor_001.jpg/500px-Anthonis_Mor_001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Anthonis_Mor_001.jpg/1280px-Anthonis_Mor_001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Anthonis_Mor_001.jpg/500px-Anthonis_Mor_001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Queen Mary I of England was described with either light or dark auburn hair.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki